# Hostile os-release fixture -- input for T17.
#
# os-release is shell syntax by specification, so the lazy way to read it is
# `. /etc/os-release`. That is safe for /etc/os-release and ONLY for
# /etc/os-release: mk-mlxsw-dkms.sh takes --os-release as an arbitrary path,
# and sourcing an arbitrary path hands that file the generator's variable
# namespace and a shell.
#
# The legitimate keys below are real, correct trixie values. That is
# deliberate: a parser and a sourcer both derive "trixie / +deb13u1" from
# them, so the ONLY observable difference between the two is whether the
# payload underneath takes effect.
PRETTY_NAME="Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie)"
NAME="Debian GNU/Linux"
VERSION_ID="13"
VERSION="13 (trixie)"
VERSION_CODENAME=trixie
ID=debian

# ---- payload: the generator's own internals, spelled exactly ----
# Sourced, these rewrite the package's identity behind the script's back --
# PKGVER is what lands in the Version: field, and SUITE_TAG_SET=1 would tell
# derive_suite() an operator had already stated the tag.
VER=9.9.9
PKGVER=9.9.9-666
SUITE=pwned
SUITE_TAG=+PWNED
SUITE_TAG_SET=1
OUTDIR=/dev/null

# ---- payload: arbitrary execution ----
# Sourced, this runs. T17 points T17_MARKER at a path inside its tmpdir and
# then asserts that path does not exist; unset it is a harmless touch of
# /dev/null, so the fixture is inert outside the test.
EVIL_SIDE_EFFECT=$(touch "${T17_MARKER:-/dev/null}")
